 "text": "The flawed v zero constructor returns an empty H T T P client: no connect timeout, no response-header timeout, no total. A node that accepts a connection and never answers holds the request and its goroutine indefinitely. At lesson zero two, the same function now builds its client from three numbers: two hundred milliseconds to dial, two and a half seconds for response headers, and two and a half seconds for the whole exchange. That is a per-attempt budget; a hang becomes an error the gateway answers with a five oh four. At v one hardened, the deadlines stay, and reads gain a bounded retry policy: at most two retries, backoff capped at four hundred milliseconds, only while retries stay under ten percent of node calls. Writes are never retried. Every line shown comes from one of the three pinned commits.",
